# tools/runpod_nvidia_sm89.env -- THE ONE ORDERED sm_89 RUNPOD WALK (2026-11-05).
# Read by tools/prebuild_changed.py --rent (parsed: GPU_WALK["sm_89"] and the GPU-count walk) and sourced by
# tools/nvidia_central.sh, whose `up` defaults to the MEASUREMENT walk below. Change it here only.
# Plain KEY="value" lines, no shell expansion, so Python reads them without a shell.
#
# Only sm_89 GPUs: every Mojolearn release carries cuda sm_89 and sm_90a only, so an sm_86 pod (RTX A6000,
# A40) runs our arm on nothing, and a prebuild's keys are partitioned by device arch. Counts are tried in
# order, each over every type: 0.8.66 prebuild asked for 1x sm_89 only and saw no stock for 2 h while
# nvidia_central got 4x RTX 4090. NVIDIA only; no Apple machine type ever belongs here.
NVIDIA_SM89_GPUS="NVIDIA GeForce RTX 4090,NVIDIA L40S,NVIDIA RTX 6000 Ada Generation,NVIDIA L4"
NVIDIA_SM89_GPU_COUNTS="4 2 1"
# THE MEASUREMENT POD (2026-11-13): tools/nvidia_central.sh up asks for these only. The paper's NVIDIA device is the
# L40S and Andrew's rule is "compare on the same device" (AMD: MI300X only); the sm_89 walk above rented a 2x RTX 6000
# Ada when the L40S was out of stock. One GPU: the timed boards use one (tools/ops/paper_compare_job.sh, serial by
# nature) and the smoke shards are host-bound. MOJOLEARN_NVC_GPUS / NVC_GPU_COUNTS override it explicitly.
NVIDIA_MEASURE_GPUS="NVIDIA L40S"
NVIDIA_MEASURE_GPU_COUNTS="1"
